### 1. What It Is
List Virtualization (Windowing) is a high-performance rendering technique that calculates the visible viewport window and mounts only the DOM elements currently visible to the user (plus a small overscan buffer), recycling DOM nodes as the user scrolls.

### 2. Why It Exists & Historical Motivation
Mounting 10,000 DOM rows in the browser causes severe DOM bloat, high memory consumption (hundreds of megabytes of DOM nodes), sluggish reflows, and slow initial render times.

### 3. What Problem It Solves
Scales lists from 10 items to 1,000,000 items with constant $O(1)$ DOM nodes (~20–40 nodes), guaranteed 60fps scrolling, and minimal memory footprints.

### 4. Prerequisites
